       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the labeled maximum daily dose for adults, which is 10 mg. The patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit. A dose this high risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock.\n\nPlease check whether 50 mg was a typo. These are some options:\n- **5 mg orally once daily**, the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg orally once daily**, the maximum dose.\n\nIf you want me to enter either dose, tell me which. If you need more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, adding a second agent from another class, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, is the usual approach. Pharmacy or the attending can help choose one."
